  "outcome_rule": "at t = 120 tu: k = round(mass / one Orbium's mass); k 0 'both die', 1 'one dies', 2 and one connected component of A > 0.01 on the torus 'fused into one bound pair', 2 otherwise 'both survive, scattered'; 'detonation' if fill (A > 0.1) > 0.25 or mass > 6 x",
  "caveats": [
    "One phase of the Orbium and one starting gap (5 R) per geometry; outcomes of Lenia collisions depend on phase and exact offset, so each panel is one sample, not the outcome for that angle.",
    "Single runs, alm only, R13 T10, 256^2 torus: after a collision, debris can wrap around and meet again.",
    "Not novel: Chan 2019 sec. 3.5.5 catalogues Orbium collision outcomes (merging, bouncing, death, detonation). This is our simulator reproducing that kind of zoo."
  ],
